      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIKI BE GOOD (11) was successful at his most recent outing by 2.25 metres in a break through win this campaign at Riverina Paceway over 1740m. Hard to know where he gets from this slightly awkward draw. Meets a comparable field and he can go right on with the job. NOVANTA RISING (10) was responsible for a far better performance at his latest appearance when he scored over 2270m at Riverina Paceway, getting home by 2 metres after leading. Tackles a similar assignment and he can make it two on the trot. LETSSTARTINHEAVEN (8) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and 99th last start over 1609m at Menangle, coming home from the winner. Interesting to see what unfolds from this wide draw he is talented enough to win from there. RUDY GEE (7) is up in grade but came from wider to win fresh at Newcastle, his third success from his last four starts. Go well again.",
